{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>To You</b> — He relates that he found nothing to do but to call and supplicate and say: What profit is in my death?! For the blood is the life [הנפש], and it is written: ושרט לנפש [\"and he shall cut for the life/soul\"]."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {0 "Ibn Ezra alludes to Leviticus 19:28 (ושרט לנפש) and the identification of blood with the life principle (cf. Deut. 12:23); the argument is left terse as in the original."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:28:59.546173036Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}